      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T09:03:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we handle the shared tail rather than return success here? If the datagram ends inside a shared buffer, this leaves the trailer attached, so cloned packets can still exhibit the oversized-frame behavior this change fixes. Please make the affected tail private before trimming, handle allocation failure explicitly, and add coverage for a cloned chain.",
      "revId": "6237005e9df5da3e0c3817fddaf348a4ac2bd5c5",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
    },
    {
